# Git remotes (mandatory)

## Continuity product (default / `main`)

**`origin` must be:** `https://github.com/audiohacking/h3-ws`

- Web UI on `:8765`, `server.py`, Continuity-inspired standalone port powered by h3.c.
- Before every `git push` on Continuity work: `git remote -v` → confirm `origin` is `audiohacking/h3-ws`.
- Fix if wrong: `git remote set-url origin https://github.com/audiohacking/h3-ws.git`

## Live experiment (set aside)

**`fasth3-live` remote only:** `https://github.com/audiohacking/FastH3-Live-MLX`

- FastH3 Live stream / Metal decode experiments — learning branch, not the product mainline.
- Never push Continuity/`main` work there. Never make this `origin` while doing Continuity features.
- Push Live work only with an explicit `git push fasth3-live …`.

## Anti-footgun

- Do not push to a repo that is not the active product for the current branch.
- A mistaken cross-push is a critical incident: revert that remote’s `main`/tags to the pre-push SHA immediately.
